  "footer_blank_columns_note": "the slaves block, six of the seven industry columns, the pensioners block, every deaf/dumb/blind/insane column, every coloured column and every schools column carry no figure at the foot of this sheet and no entry on any of its 31 lines. Only TOTAL and MANUFACTURES AND TRADES are footed.",
  "footer_total_glyph_note": "the TOTAL footing is three figures. The first is a single bold ascending slash — this hand's 1. The second and third are the same glyph as each other: a hook rising to the upper right, then a crescent bowl curling below and left. That is the form 33S7-9YYJ-B1 carries eleven times over as a labelled 3 (its line 1 at y676 and its line 3 at y830 are the same two strokes), and it is NOT this hand's 5, whose top stroke is a LONG HORIZONTAL BAR drawn to the right as far as the column rule — lines 14, 16, 21, 27, 28 and 29 of this sheet write that bar and the footing does not. Read 133.",
  "footer_manufactures_glyph_note": "a single figure 7 in the manufactures and trades column, drawn across the closing rule; the sheet carries seven entries in that column and they close to it exactly."
