  "state": "unpaired",
  "why": "a continuation sheet carries no name and no printed page number of its own, so the pairing to its left sheet is a separate reading: the page population below has to be matched against the printed age-band totals at the foot of each candidate left sheet. T-0642 does that for all eleven at once and left this sheet `unpaired_key_not_yet_read` because no footing had been read from it; this file supplies the footing. Recorded as unpaired rather than guessed.",
  "page_population_key": 133,
  "page_population_key_note": "the printed footer figure, which is what a left sheet's age-band sums are to be matched against. The line-by-line reading of the same column is 114, and the two do NOT agree, so the printed figure is the one to pair on and the residual is carried with it. None of the six candidate left sheets T-0642 lists for this leaf (printed populations 103, 208, 146, 160, 182 and 152) stands at either figure, so this key does not close the pairing on its own.",
